Every verb ley knows is in this build. What is planned next lives in
docs/plans/build-order.md; the Mac app is the next milestone.

Recording is in this build:

  ley record <freq>        write what the radio hears to a file
  ley recordings           what has been recorded
  ley recordings path <id> where a recording is, for Finder or another tool

Decoding is in this build:

  ley decoders             the installed decoder plugins
  ley decode <name>        run one and print what it hears
  ley records              search what kept jobs wrote
  ley track <protocol>     the live entity table
  ley watch <name> ...     filter records, and notify on a match

Still to come there: 'ley label' and 'ley devices-seen', and 'ley
identify'.

The daemon-side relative squelch (mute at 'noise floor + N dB' measured by
the daemon rather than by ley) is the recorded follow-up to auto squelch.
